#!/usr/bin/python3
"""tandem-mixer: a hover mixer for waybar's audio module (replaces pavucontrol).

Hover (or click) waybar's audio module and a mixer drops down under it:
  OUTPUT  the default output's volume, and every output device (click one to switch to it)
  APPS    every app playing on the laptop: volume per app, play/pause for media players (MPRIS)
  MIC     the default input's volume
  PHONE   while tandem links the phone: the phone's players (play/pause) + media volume,
          or its Bluetooth stream when the laptop has the headphones
Click any percentage to mute/unmute. Scrolling the bar module still changes volume (waybar).

Waybar has no hover hook, so the waybar-hover CFFI module (waybar-hover.so) runs inside waybar,
hooks the audio module's widget, and reports enter/leave/click + position over a unix socket.
It also shows a small phone icon next to the volume while audio is shared with the phone.

Usage: tandem-mixer                   run (user service)
       tandem-mixer --setup-waybar    add the hover module to waybar, drop on-click pavucontrol
       tandem-mixer --restore-waybar  undo --setup-waybar
       tandem-mixer --toggle          open/close the mixer (for keybinds)
       tandem-mixer --demo [--np]     fake data, always open (screenshots; --np: only the bar pill)
"""
